 "instruction": "The held-out divergence guard in `luthi/v2/jepa_runner.py` (`JEPATrainer._check_divergence`) kills a run whenever a modality's `nmse_mean` exceeds `divergence_nmse_max`. Under a combined next-token + JEPA objective, NMSE alone isn't sufficient evidence that a run is broken: runs have been killed at marginal NMSE while generating well.\n\nAdd a two-gauge rule:\n\n- New `RunnerConfig` field `divergence_ppl_veto: float = 0.0` (0 = off).\n- When the veto is > 0 and the same held-out result for that modality reports a finite `perplexity` below the veto, an NMSE trip is vetoed. Log it loudly at error level and don't return a kill reason for that modality.\n- Behavior is unchanged when the veto is 0, or when perplexity is missing, non-finite, or at or above the veto. A non-finite NMSE is never vetoed. The separate 10x-loss guard is untouched.\n\nAlso wire it into `scripts/jepa_pilot_driver.py`: add an `ARM_PPL_VETO` dict giving 8000.0 for the arms `probe_d8_llmjepa` and `probe_d8_llmjepa6k`, pass it into the runner config (default 0.0 for other arms), and record it in the run's saved config.",
